@startuml sequence-admin-ops-m23
title SEQ-09: Administration, Audit & Operational Support Flow (UC-11 / UC-12 / UC-13 / UC-14 / UC-15)
autonumber
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

actor "Administrator" as Admin
actor "Operations Staff" as Ops
boundary "Web Admin Portal\n(SCR-A-07..SCR-A-11)" as AdminUI
control "Admin Service\n(Route Handler / BFF)" as AdminSvc
control "Support Service\n(Operations Handler)" as SupportSvc
database "PostgreSQL Database\n(Core Schema)" as DB
entity "AuditLog Store\n(Append-Only Ledger)" as Audit

note over AdminUI, DB
    Architectural Note: Admin endpoint paths (/api/admin/*) represent illustrative
    Next.js Route Handler / BFF design mappings, not frozen cross-framework wire contracts.
end note

== 1. Account & Role Administration (UC-11) ==
Admin -> AdminUI: Manage user roles at User Center (SCR-A-07)
activate AdminUI
Admin -> AdminUI: Select user, assign new role (e.g. MODERATOR, ORG_MANAGER) & enter justification
AdminUI -> AdminSvc: PATCH /api/admin/users/{userId}/role { role: "MODERATOR", reason: text }
activate AdminSvc

alt Target is Last Administrator and Demoting Role
    AdminSvc --> AdminUI: 400 Bad Request (SECURITY_LAST_ADMIN_PROTECTED)
    AdminUI --> Admin: Error: Cannot remove the last Administrator
else Valid Role Modification
    AdminSvc -> DB: UPDATE "Profile" SET role = 'MODERATOR' WHERE id = targetUserId
    activate DB
    DB --> AdminSvc: Role updated
    deactivate DB

    AdminSvc -> Audit: INSERT INTO "AuditLog" (\n  action = 'ROLE_CHANGE', actorId = auth.uid(),\n  targetId = targetUserId, details = JSONB, timestamp = now()\n)
    activate Audit
    Audit --> AdminSvc: Audit entry recorded
    deactivate Audit

    AdminSvc --> AdminUI: 200 OK { updated: true }
    AdminUI --> Admin: Role updated successfully & audit recorded
end
deactivate AdminSvc

== 2. Operational Reporting (UC-12) ==
Admin -> AdminUI: Open Operational Analytics Dashboard (SCR-A-08)
AdminUI -> AdminSvc: GET /api/admin/reports/system-analytics?timeframe=30d
activate AdminSvc
AdminSvc -> DB: Query Aggregated Metrics View:\n- Active Learners count\n- Course/Lesson Completion Rates\n- Daily Streak Retention Rates
activate DB
DB --> AdminSvc: Return aggregated analytics dataset
deactivate DB
AdminSvc --> AdminUI: 200 OK { metrics: [...] }
deactivate AdminSvc
AdminUI --> Admin: Render System Charts & Operational KPI cards

== 3. Security Audit Log Inspection (UC-13) ==
Admin -> AdminUI: Open Security Audit Log Viewer (SCR-A-09)
AdminUI -> AdminSvc: GET /api/admin/audit-logs?action=ROLE_CHANGE&limit=50
activate AdminSvc
AdminSvc -> Audit: SELECT * FROM "AuditLog" WHERE action = 'ROLE_CHANGE'\nORDER BY timestamp DESC LIMIT 50 (illustrative query limit, configurable)\n(Append-Only Store: Zero Update / Zero Delete APIs exist)
activate Audit
Audit --> AdminSvc: Return immutable audit log records
deactivate Audit
AdminSvc --> AdminUI: 200 OK { auditLogs: [...] }
deactivate AdminSvc
AdminUI --> Admin: Display Audit Trail with timestamps, actor IDs, and immutable proofs

== 4. Support Ticket Handling (UC-14 / BF-15) ==
Ops -> AdminUI: Open Support Operations Queue (SCR-A-10)
AdminUI -> SupportSvc: GET /api/admin/support/tickets?status=OPEN
activate SupportSvc
SupportSvc -> DB: SELECT * FROM "SupportTicket" WHERE status = 'OPEN'
activate DB
DB --> SupportSvc: Return open support tickets
deactivate DB
SupportSvc --> AdminUI: 200 OK { tickets: [...] }
deactivate SupportSvc

Ops -> AdminUI: Inspect ticket details (minimal user lookup, zero password/private data)
alt Operational Resolution
    Ops -> AdminUI: Submit resolution notes & mark RESOLVED
    AdminUI -> SupportSvc: PATCH /api/admin/support/tickets/{id} { status: "RESOLVED", resolutionNotes }
    activate SupportSvc
    SupportSvc -> DB: UPDATE "SupportTicket" SET status = 'RESOLVED' WHERE id = ticketId
    activate DB
    DB --> SupportSvc: Ticket updated
    deactivate DB
    SupportSvc --> AdminUI: 200 OK
    deactivate SupportSvc
else Escalation Required (Content Error -> Moderator | Security -> Admin)
    Ops -> AdminUI: Escalate ticket to target role with reference
    AdminUI -> SupportSvc: POST /api/admin/support/tickets/{id}/escalate { targetRole: "MODERATOR" }
    activate SupportSvc
    SupportSvc -> DB: UPDATE "SupportTicket" SET assignedRole = 'MODERATOR', status = 'ESCALATED'
    activate DB
    DB --> SupportSvc: Ticket escalated
    deactivate DB
    SupportSvc --> AdminUI: 200 OK
    deactivate SupportSvc
end

== 5. Optional B2B Cohort Extension Boundary (UC-15) ==
note over AdminUI, DB
    UC-15 / MVP-17 Extension Boundary Marker:
    - B2B Cohort & Group Management operates strictly as an isolated extension.
    - Zero dependencies from Core Learner progression or B2C flows.
    - No Core contract surfaces are impacted.
end note
deactivate AdminUI

@enduml
